# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Tool Finder — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. DATABASE_URL (a postgres:// URL) is REQUIRED;
# everything else is optional in development — production requires the
# variables marked REQUIRED.
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for the full platform walkthrough (Netlify/Vercel + Neon,
# Supabase, Railway/Render, Docker).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (PostgreSQL only — Neon / Supabase / Railway / Render / local) ─
# DATABASE_URL        → the POOLED connection (Neon :6543 / Supabase :6544)
#                       with ?sslmode=require&connection_limit=1 — used by
#                       the app at runtime.
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL → the direct connection (:5432), used by
#                       prisma migrate / db push (`pnpm db:setup`).
#                       OPTIONAL for Neon: when it's missing, the direct host
#                       is derived from the pooled URL automatically (strip
#                       `-pooler`, port 5432 — see prisma.config.ts). Set it
#                       explicitly for Supabase/other hosts.
# DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@ep-xyz-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech:6543/neondb?sslmode=require&connection_limit=1"
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@ep-xyz.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech:5432/neondb?sslmode=require"

# ── Admin dashboard ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED in production — the dashboard fails closed without both.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD must be 48+ characters; generate ADMIN_SECRET with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# (In development the demo password from the sign-in screen is used.)
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
# ADMIN_SECRET=""

# ── Public site URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No trailing slash. Drives emails, sitemap, Open Graph and canonical URLs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://yourdomain.com"

# ── Email (optional — dry-run without a key) ─────────────────────────────────
# With RESEND_API_KEY set, admin replies and password-reset links are emailed.
# Without it the app logs emails to the server console (dry-run mode) and the
# reset link is returned by the API so the demo stays usable.
# RESEND_API_KEY=""
# RESEND_FROM="AI Tool Finder <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# CONTACT_REPLY_TO="editors@yourdomain.com"

# ── Donations (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real donation page for the "Support us" button (demo flow otherwise).
# DONATE_PROVIDER_URL="https://ko-fi.com/yourpage"

# ── Source package endpoint (GET /api/download) ──────────────────────────────
# Development: public by default. Production: requires an admin session
# (fail closed). Override explicitly if you need to:
# SOURCE_DOWNLOAD_PUBLIC="true"    # anyone may download the source zip
# SOURCE_DOWNLOAD_PUBLIC="false"   # admin-only, even in development

# ── Local production server (pnpm build && pnpm start) ──────────────────────
# The standalone server honours PORT and HOSTNAME (exported from this file by
# scripts/start-production.sh). HOSTNAME binds the interface:
#   127.0.0.1 → only this machine can open the site (recommended default)
#   0.0.0.0   → other devices on your LAN can reach it (firewall will prompt)
# PORT="3000"
# HOSTNAME="127.0.0.1"
# For a local machine deployment walkthrough see DEPLOY-MACOS.md.
